items/thm-cantor-normal-form.md:71:[L6] $\mu^{+}$ is an ordinal; $\bigcup A$ is an ordinal and the least upper bound of a set $A$ of ordinals; $\mu \subseteq \nu$ iff $\mu \in \nu$ or $\mu = \nu$; $\mu \notin \mu$ ([[lem-ordinal-basics]]); hence $\mu < \nu$ iff $\mu^{+} \le \nu$. Exactly one of $\mu \in \nu$, $\mu = \nu$, $\nu \in \mu$ holds, and every nonempty set of ordinals has an $\in$-least element ([[lem-ordinal-trichotomy]]).
items/ex-a-singular-cardinal-of-uncountable-cofinality.md:68:[L9] Ordinals satisfy trichotomy; $\alpha \subseteq \beta$ iff $\alpha \in \beta$ or $\alpha = \beta$; the union of a set of ordinals is its least upper bound; every nonempty set of ordinals has an $\in$-least element; and every strictly increasing map of ordinals is injective ([[lem-ordinal-trichotomy]], [[lem-ordinal-basics]], [[def-injection-surjection-bijection]]).
items/ex-the-beth-hierarchy-computed.md:68:[L7] $\omega$ is a limit ordinal; ordinals satisfy trichotomy, the union of a set of ordinals is its least upper bound, $\alpha \subseteq \beta$ iff $\alpha \in \beta$ or $\alpha = \beta$, and every strictly increasing map of ordinals is injective ([[lem-omega-least-limit-ordinal]], [[lem-ordinal-basics]], [[lem-ordinal-trichotomy]], [[def-injection-surjection-bijection]]).
