items/thm-ordinal-arithmetic-monotonicity.md:89:[L3] $\mu^{+}$ is an ordinal; $\bigcup A$ is an ordinal and is the least upper bound of any set $A$ of ordinals; $\mu \subseteq \nu$ if and only if $\mu \in \nu$ or $\mu = \nu$; and $\mu \notin \mu$ (claims (b), (c), (e), (f) of [[lem-ordinal-basics]]).
items/thm-ordinal-arithmetic-monotonicity.md:143:**No completeness is assumed.** Every supremum here is a union of a set of ordinals, an ordinal by claim (e) of [[lem-ordinal-basics]]. The ordinals are closed under suprema of sets for free, which is what makes the limit clauses legitimate in the first place.
items/cor-cofinality-of-a-cardinal-power.md:71:[L10] Ordinals satisfy trichotomy, $\alpha \subseteq \beta$ iff $\alpha \in \beta$ or $\alpha = \beta$, the union of a set of ordinals is its least upper bound, and every nonempty set of ordinals has an $\in$-least element; a function is injective when equality of two values forces equality of the corresponding inputs ([[lem-ordinal-trichotomy]], [[lem-ordinal-basics]], [[def-well-order]], [[def-injection-surjection-bijection]]).
items/thm-regularity-of-the-alephs.md:75:[L9] Ordinals satisfy trichotomy, $\alpha \subseteq \beta$ iff $\alpha \in \beta$ or $\alpha = \beta$, the union of a set of ordinals is its least upper bound, every nonempty set of ordinals has an $\in$-least element, $\omega$ is the least limit ordinal, and every strictly increasing map of ordinals is injective ([[lem-ordinal-trichotomy]], [[lem-ordinal-basics]], [[lem-omega-least-limit-ordinal]], [[def-injection-surjection-bijection]]).

